From f07fb492612b80c9773d61c7b3c3e5c55b147de0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 09:10:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Opt-in-off consumers: a skill, DMN or todo store a mount left
 out is not judged here

In a root that mounts cat-harness without its opt-in groups (sdlc,
work-plan, editorial, kg-ops, platform-ui: smart-ips-pilgrimage#66's
lock), five gates failed on content absent by consent, not by defect
(owner cards Q-OPTIN-DIRS A and Q-SKILL-TOOL-LINK B: a target in a
switched-off group is judged where the group is on):

- scripts/lib/switched-off-skills.ts (new): switchedOffSkillHomes and
  judgeSkillRef, moved from check-tools.ts (re-exported there, its
  messages unchanged), so check:tools, check:workflow-refs and kg:audit
  answer one skill name the same way. A group the mount LEFT OUT is no
  longer unknowable: the layer's committed skill index (SKILLS.md, else
  the AGENTS.md region), which readme:sync writes with every opt-in group
  marked and the layer's own CI keeps current, names its skills, so they
  are HELD there by name for any referring layer. A left-out group the
  index does not list keeps the narrower own-layer pass.
- check:workflow-refs: 70 refs (todo-manager, bean-coordination,
  rendered-impact, ...) from fhir-harness, folio-assistant-core and
  smart-trust-tools diagrams into cat-harness's left-out groups are
  reported as not judged here instead of DANGLING.
- kg:audit role-skills-resolve: the same for a role's skills.
- kg:audit test-plan-resolves: an exit DMN in a left-out group
  (sdlc/processes/decisions/test-certification.dmn) is not judged
  (dmnRefSwitchedOff); a missing one in a group switched on still is.
- readme:sync skills:index: a left-out group's sections are kept verbatim
  from the committed index, in place, so the layer's SKILLS.md and
  AGENTS.md no longer read stale in a mount (and kind:register:check,
  which runs readme:sync:check, passes).
- state:visualizer: a published todos projection whose store is
  determined absent (StoreAbsentError, smart-ips-pilgrimage#13) renders a
  page saying so instead of crashing the run; any other failure to
  resolve the store still throws.

Verified in a tree composed from smart-ips-pilgrimage#66's lock
(mount-from-lock, state:mount): state:visualizer:check (with a todos
projection), check:workflow-refs, readme:sync:check, kg:audit:check,
kind:register:check and check:tools all exit 0, where the first five
exited 1 before. Six new cases in optin-mounting-root.test.ts (15 pass);
tsc --noEmit clean; the other touched suites fail the same way with and
without this change in a mount (environment), and one more passes.

